# WhitecardVision — CSS structure (ValeSpec style)

Applies to first-party stylesheets under `WhitecardVision/`. **Exclude** `WhitecardVision/00__ThirdParty__**/`.

## File header

Use a `/* … */` block with `= ` rule lines and fields: **FILE**, **NAMESPACE** (`Wv`), **MODULE**, **PURPOSE**, and **DESCRIPTION** when the sheet covers multiple features.

## Regions (block comments)

- Opening trio (same width as `ValeSpec__ProductIndex__Styles__Main__.css`):

  `/* ----------------------------------------------------------------- */`  
  `/* REGION | Short Title (pad so title ends near column 70)      */`  
  `/* ----------------------------------------------------------------- */`

- Close each region: `/* endregion ----------------------------------------------------------------- */` (flush left, not indented).

- **Indent rules inside a region** with **4 spaces** before selectors; **8 spaces** before declarations so nested blocks read like ValeSpec Product Index.

- Use `/* Section Name: … */` before clusters of related selectors when it helps scan-ability (optional; use where the region has multiple sub-areas).

## Declarations

- **Align colons** in a column within each rule block: pad between property name and `:` (Vale hand-formatting).
- **Logical property order** within a rule: `display` / `position` → box model → typography → paint → misc.
- Prefer **existing `var(--Wv__…`)** tokens from `WhitecardVision__CoreUi__Styles__Variables__.css`; keep **fallbacks** in `var()` when shared components still use legacy token names (e.g. templates panel fallbacks).

## Reference

- `WebApps/ValeSpec/02__Src__AppModules/50__System__ProductIndex/ValeSpec__ProductIndex__Styles__Main__.css`
- `WebApps/Whitecardopedia/03__Style__AppStylesheets/Na__CoreUi__Styles__Variables__.css` (block-comment `* REGION` variant; Whitecard uses the ProductIndex dash style for consistency with ValeSpec first-party Wv modules).

## Anti-patterns

- Dropping the close `/* endregion … */` so regions are unclosed.
- Mixing `=====` section banners in new work when the file already uses the ProductIndex `/* REGION | … */` pattern (keep one convention per file).
